#X obj 659 11 noise.chua~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 356 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A digital emulation of Chua's diode circuit — a classic
example of a simple electronic circuit that exhibits chaotic behavior.
The generator produces two correlated chaotic audio signals \, X and
Y \, whose shape depends on the circuit parameters: capacitance @C1
\, capacitance @C2 \, inductance @L and resistance @R. Different parameter
combinations produce periodic \, quasi-periodic or fully chaotic waveforms.;
#X text 240 214 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 239 • Chaotic audio source — feeding the outputs directly
into a mixer or effect chain to obtain evolving \, unpredictable noise
textures.;
#X text 250 294 • Modulation source — using the X or Y signal as a
chaotic control source for filter cutoff \, pan or pitch \, to obtain
organic and evolving movement.;
#X text 250 349 • Chaotic modulation of parameters — slowly changing
the circuit parameters (@R \, @L \, @C1 \, @C2) to make the output
transition between periodic and chaotic regimes over time.;
